# Hot-path performance

Ashenwake combat must stay bounded under pack + overlapping-AoE stress. Do not reintroduce per-frame scans, unique materials, or unbounded `new()`/`queue_free()` on hit/tick/FX paths.

## Pools and lifecycle

- Pool repeating FX, labels, and projectiles. Warm up in `Arena._ready`. Steal oldest when full; never grow unbounded.
- Prune with `is_instance_valid` before reuse. Arena reload must not leave the static pool pointing at freed nodes.
- Cap spawn rate (token bucket). Dropping a visual must not drop damage, status, or meter.

## Geometry and materials

- Build CPU meshes once (spawn / hop reveal). Do not `SurfaceTool.commit()` every `_process`.
- Snapshot NPC endpoints. Follow only `GameSession.active_unit` origins, and only at ~10 Hz.
- Share `ShaderMaterial` / particle resources. Cache split-color combat-text materials; never one unique material per label.

## Simulation and queries

- Use `ArenaState.units_near(point, radius)` instead of scanning `ArenaState.units`.
- Batch same-source same-window procs (shock chains) and keep summed damage. Time-slice AoE pulses and chain flushes with a per-physics-frame budget.
- One runner ticks many instances. Do not give each damage number, bolt, or meter row its own `_process`.

## HUD and combat text

- Index live combat text (periodic / cast / queue). Do not linear-scan `_live` on every hit.
- Throttle HUD rebuilds (~10 Hz). Dirty-flag, then refresh.

## When adding a system

Ask: what is the 60-dummy × 5-AoE cost? If it is `O(zones × units × hops)` per tick or allocates per hit, batch, index, pool, or budget it before shipping.

Reference implementations: `thunder_wave_fx.gd`, `damage_number.gd`, `ground_aoe_fx.gd`, `arena_state.units_near`, shock-chain flush on `unit.gd`.
